  "title": "fix round 1 for T-1518: write the four acceptance-named tests (grace turns, short line after handover, default threshold when key absent, CLI forwards --session-id)",
  "spec": "Fix round for T-1518 (goal T-1515, H2v2), branch cut from task/T-1518 (commit 5ff15fe implemented planner_context.user_turns, the [planner].handover_grace_turns grace, DEFAULT_HANDOVER_CONTEXT_TOKENS, the handover-session.json nag-once record, handover.write(reason, session_id=, tokens_at=) and the cli --session-id forwarding). The gate held it gate_red because none of the four acceptance-named tests exist (`missing: test not defined`); the executor changed 2 lines of tests.\n\nWrite exactly these four tests, named exactly like this, as unittest.TestCase methods next to the existing tests in each file, using the same fixtures (tests/test_planner_context.py builds a projects dir with transcripts and a cfg dict; tests/test_cli.py patches sys.argv and the planner_context / handover functions). Behaviour under test is the T-1518 spec (read bus task T-1518 for the full contract):\n1. tests/test_planner_context.py::test_hook_message_grace_turns_suppresses_early_handover: a transcript over the threshold with 3 user prompt records (plus tool_result records, which must not count) and cfg planner.handover_grace_turns 12 -> hook_message returns None; the same transcript with 12 user prompt records -> the full instruction, and it contains '--session-id'; the legacy path (no transcript, no session_id) ignores the grace.\n2. tests/test_planner_context.py::test_hook_message_short_line_after_handover_for_this_session: after handover.write('context', session_id=S, tokens_at=T) (ROOT patched to a tempdir so .orchestrator/checkpoint/handover-session.json lands there), hook_message for session S whose transcript reports T + 1000 tokens returns a line starting 'handover written' that does not contain 'hand over now'; a different session id gets the full instruction; a transcript at T + 30000 (over handover_regrow_tokens 20000) gets the full instruction.\n3. tests/test_planner_context.py::test_default_threshold_when_key_absent: cfg without handover_context_tokens: a 310000-token transcript with enough user prompts returns the instruction, a 290000-token one returns None; with the key set to 0 hook_message returns None for any size.\n4. tests/test_cli.py::test_handover_cli_forwards_session_id: `orchestrator handover --reason context --session-id S` calls handover.write with session_id 'S' and tokens_at an int or None (handover.write and planner_context.context_tokens patched); `planner-context --hook --session-id S` prints a line containing '--session-id S' when hook_message (patched to return the instruction built for S) is over threshold.\n\nIf a test exposes a defect in the implementation, fix it in the three source files (in scope) and say so in the result. Do not rename or weaken existing tests. Commit first, then run tests/test_planner_context.py tests/test_cli.py tests/test_handover.py in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate.",
